spots.t:
List the 15 best things to do in and around {CITY}, {COUNTRY}, most important first. Lean toward the most popular, best-reviewed places. Include at least 3 evening options (sunset spots, evening strolls, shows), at least 2 indoor options for a rainy or too-hot afternoon, and a day trip if there is a classic one. If it is a large region or island, give options in each main area so a day can stay in one area. Do not include trains, transfers or transport as activities. Travelers' interests: anything. Travelers' ages: adults.
Reply with JSON only: {"d":"what {CITY} is known for, one sentence","lat":0,"lng":0,"spots":[{"n":"name","d":"what it is or what it is known for, one short sentence","t":["tag"],"fame":1,"rating":4.6,"k":0,"s":"am","dur":"2h","ticket":"Free","pic":"oldtown","place":"the real place","lat":0,"lng":0}]}
place = the exact name of the real place, as on its sign or on a map (for an outing such as a stroll, a tasting or a cruise, the real place where it happens, e.g. 'Piazza Duomo' or 'Marina Grande'); never an invented or descriptive name. n may be descriptive, place may not. pic = the picture that fits best, one of: beach, island, mountain, gorge, ruins, temple, church, museum, castle, oldtown, harbor, park, garden, market, viewpoint, lake, waterfall, cave, nightlife, themepark, zoo, spa, vineyard, bridge, square. s = best time: am, pm, eve, or any (a full-day outing). dur = the recommended time to spend there for these travelers, e.g. '45m', '1-2h', 'half day' or 'full day'. ticket = 'Free', or price and whether to book ahead, e.g. '€18, book ahead'. Use accurate coordinates. Tags (t) only from: relax,adventure,food,beach,mountain,culture,nature,nightlife,shopping,family,wellness,scenic. k: 1 = great for small kids, 0 = fine, -1 = better for older kids and adults. fame = 2 for the essential must-sees most visitors come for (a city's top handful), 1 for popular, well-known places, 0 for hidden gems and local favorites most visitors miss. rating = its typical visitor review score out of 5 on Google or Tripadvisor, one decimal (0 if you do not know). Only suggest places that are consistently well reviewed (about 4.3 or more); never a tourist trap.

food.t:
List 15 places to eat in {CITY}, {COUNTRY}: the best-loved local classics, casual spots, a couple of special dinners, and at least 4 breakfast cafés or bakeries, spread across the city or region. Travelers' interests: anything. Travelers' ages: adults.
Reply with JSON only: {"transit":{"system":"how public transit works and what a ticket costs, one sentence","pass":"best pass or card for visitors","airport":"how to get from the main airport or station to the center","tip":"one practical tip"},"stay":[{"n":"neighborhood","d":"why stay here, short","lat":0,"lng":0}],"food":[{"n":"name","d":"what it is known for or what to order, one short sentence","fame":1,"rating":4.5,"cuisine":"","price":"€€","meal":"both","dur":"1h","fav":false,"k":0,"sure":true,"reserve":false,"pic":"taverna","lat":0,"lng":0}]}
pic = the picture that fits best, one of: pasta, pizza, seafood, grill, taverna, cafe, bakery, gelato, streetfood, wine, sushi, noodles, tacos, curry, deli. reserve = true if booking a table ahead is recommended. meal = breakfast, lunch, dinner, both (lunch and dinner) or all (all three). dur = the recommended time to allow for a meal there, e.g. '30m' for a bakery, '1-1.5h' for a sit-down lunch, '2h' for a long dinner. fav = true for places food lovers seek out (a famous classic, a top market, a destination restaurant). Use real places and accurate coordinates. n = the exact name on its sign: never a name made from the kind of place and the town ('Pasticceria Positano', 'Elounda Gelato'), never an area's places as one entry ('Plaka seaside tavernas'). sure = false when you are not certain the place exists under this exact name in this town (it may have closed, or you may be thinking of a place somewhere else), true otherwise; a place you are unsure of may still be listed, marked so. k: 1 = very family friendly, 0 = fine, -1 = adults-oriented. fame = 2 for the essential famous institutions visitors seek out, 1 for popular, well-known places, 0 for neighborhood places locals love. rating = its typical visitor review score out of 5 on Google or Tripadvisor, one decimal (0 if you do not know). Only suggest places that are consistently well reviewed (about 4.3 or more); never a tourist trap. Give 4 stay neighborhoods.
